      "title": "A Cognitive Model of the Antecedents and Consequences of Satisfaction Decisions",
      "abstract": "<jats:p> A model is proposed which expresses consumer satisfaction as a function of expectation and expectancy disconfirmation. Satisfaction, in turn, is believed to influence attitude change and purchase intention. Results from a two-stage field study support the scheme for consumers and nonconsumers of a flu inoculation. </jats:p>",
